- No payments or trading execution.

## 18. My recommendation for how we proceed

I would not jump straight into asking a vibe-coding agent to build this entire product from a single enormous prompt.

That is likely to create inconsistent navigation, incomplete calculations and features that look implemented but do not work correctly.

We should turn this blueprint into a series of connected product specifications.

| Specification                          | What it will define                                                          |
| -------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| 1. Product architecture                | How the two environments and shared financial engine relate                  |
| 2. Navigation and interaction          | Every screen, gesture, transition and navigation behaviour                   |
| 3. Money Management specification      | Every feature, form, workflow and calculation                                |
| 4. Investment Management specification | Holdings, instruments, transactions, performance and income                  |
| 5. Voice assistant specification       | Wake word, commands, contextual understanding, confirmations and permissions |
| 6. Data and privacy specification      | Financial records, storage, calculations, export, backup and security        |
| 7. Design specification                | Visual system, mobile layouts, themes and component behaviour                |
| 8. Functional acceptance criteria      | How every feature is tested before release                                   |

My recommendation is to settle the product architecture first, then fully specify the two environments separately. This protects the central concept: two independent mobile experiences supported by one accurate financial system.

I would treat this blueprint as our working product definition, not yet the final instruction to your vibe-coding agent. The next specification should go screen by screen, explaining every screen's purpose, every visible component, every interaction and every expected result. No code is needed in that specification; it should tell the development agent exactly what to build and how it must behave.